lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106683","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106683","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106683.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106683.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-05T11:19:19Z"},"body":"```\r\n                   v start_column\r\n 1 | var string := \"test     | < start_line\r\n 2 |     test test test test |\r\n 3 |     test\"               | < end_line\r\n             ^ end_column\r\n     ^ leftmost_column\r\n          rightmost_column ^\r\n\r\n                   v start_column, leftmost_column\r\n 1 | var string := \"test\" | < start_line, end_line\r\n                        ^ end_column, rightmost_column\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think these fields are pretty useless and are really only used in one place (`test_tokenizer()`).\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n\r\n```\r\n0002     print(\"test test\r\n0003 test test test test test\r\n0004 test test test\")\r\n     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n --> Literal(String) test test\r\ntest test test test test\r\ntest test test\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter:\r\n\r\n```\r\n               vvvvvvvvvv\r\n0002     print(\"test test\r\n0003 test test test test test\r\n0004 test test test\")\r\n     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n --> Literal(String) test test\r\ntest test test test test\r\ntest test test\r\n```\r\n\r\nGDScript does not have a syntax where the boundary columns of multi-line tokens are important for parsing or error messages. Such information might be needed in markup languages ​​with ASCII tables (Markdown, reStructuredText), but probably not in scripting languages ​​with simple syntax.\r\n\r\nInstead, we could add `start_position` and `end_position` fields to be able to use `substr()` to get the source code of a token or a range of tokens. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106198#discussion_r2098322864.","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=",